<title>UK: Zeneca retreats as takeover rumours fade.</title>
<headline>Zeneca retreats as takeover rumours fade.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Zeneca Group wiped out almost all of yesterday's 20-1/2p gain as takeover rumours faded, traders said.</p>
<p>By 1046 GMT, the shares were off 17-1/2p to 1520p.  </p>
<p>&quot;There's some scrappy selling in the absence of new bid speculation,&quot; said one trader of the sharp markdown in Zeneca's shares.</p>
<p>Zeneca, a longstanding subject of takeover talk, has said it intends to remain independent in the still consolidating drug industry. Yet bid talk has been driving its shares to record for months.</p>
<p>-- Debra Sherman, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4026</p>
